Qb6 9. e5 dxe5 10. Nxc6 Qc7 11. fxe5 Nd7 12. Nd5 Qxc6 13. Bb5 {Sources:
Borough of West Ham, East Ham and Stratford Express, 10 Aug 1929; West Sussex
Gazette, 12 Sept 1929 and 18 Sept 1930; West Sussex County Times and Standard,
1 Nov 1930. The Black player's surname appears as 'Wynne', 'Wynn' or 'Winn' in
print. He was Charles Edward WYNNE, born 21 Oct 1889 (St Pancras, London),
died Dec qtr. of 1966 (Poplar, London). He was a naval officer and mariner,
based in Egypt in the 1920s, marrying Millicent BEYTS in Venice in 1923. His
son David WYNNE was a noted sculptor (see Wikipedia, which mentions his
father's full name). Game contributed by Brian Denman, biographical research
by John Saunders.} 1-0

